# Lint Fix Priority

<!-- core -->
Fixing lint violations is **mandatory** and takes **priority** over finishing unrelated work. Do not bypass checks to ship faster.

Fix, don't bypass: refactor until the linter passes. **No new inline suppressions** (`@Suppress`, `eslint-disable`, `# noqa`, `//nolint`, `#[allow(...)]` — all the same violation), and no weakening of lint or formatter config. Auto-fix first, then run the project's check command before claiming the work is done.

Lint and formatter commands are project-specific. Resolve them from the project's configured lint commands (see `.myflow/project.md`); if that file is absent, detect them from the repository's build or task configuration. This rule governs the policy, not the tool names. Pre-approved exceptions live in the project's `CONTRIBUTING.md`; do not expand that list without user approval.

<!-- /core -->

## Rules

1. **Fix, don't bypass** — Refactor or reformat code to satisfy the project's lint rules.
2. **No new suppressions** — Do not add inline suppression directives unless the user explicitly asks for that approach. Suppression syntax varies by language — `@Suppress`, `@SuppressWarnings`, `// detekt:ignore`, linter disable comments, `eslint-disable`, `# noqa`, `# type: ignore`, `//nolint`, `#[allow(...)]` — treat all of them as the same violation of this rule.
3. **No config weakening** — Do not disable rules or lower thresholds in lint or formatter configuration to make checks pass.
4. **Verify before completion** — Run the project's configured lint commands (see `.myflow/project.md`) before claiming work is done.
5. **Auto-fix first** — Run the project's configured auto-format/auto-fix command for formatting issues before manual fixes.

## Documented exceptions

Pre-approved suppressions and config deviations live in the project's contributor documentation (e.g. `CONTRIBUTING.md`). Do not expand that list without user approval.

## Examples

```
// BAD — suppressing instead of fixing
<suppress "long-function">
function processOrder() { /* 200 lines */ }

// GOOD — extract helpers until the linter passes
function processOrder() {
    validateOrder();
    chargePayment();
    notifyCustomer();
}
```

```
// BAD — disabling a rule in the lint config to silence a warning

// GOOD — rename, refactor, or restructure to satisfy the rule
```

When lint fails on your changes, stop and fix it first.
